  "title": "Measuring What Matters: A New Lens on Liquidity in U.S. Rates",
  "summary": "Liquidity is the foundation of well-functioning markets, and one of those market truths everyone talks about but few can measure directly. In U.S. institutional rates markets – where trillions of dollars change hands daily – liquidity influences not just execution costs but how efficiently markets absorb information and adjust pricing.",
